{"name":"Peat Swamp Forest","hex":"#988c75","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"peat","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Soil formed of dead but not fully decayed plants found in bog areas, often burned as fuel. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A pet, a darling; a woman."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/peat"},{"term":"swamp","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An area of wet (water-saturated), spongy (soft) land, often with trees, generally a rich ecosystem for certain plants and animals but ill-suited for many agricultural purposes.","A place or situation that is foul or where progress is difficult."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To drench or fill with water.","To overwhelm; to make too busy, or overrun the capacity of."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/swamp"},{"term":"forest","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A dense uncultivated tract of trees and undergrowth, larger than woods.","Any dense collection or amount."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cover an area with trees."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/forest"}],"entries":[{"title":"Peat swamp forest","blocks":[{"text":"Peat swamp forests are tropical moist forests where waterlogged soil prevents dead leaves and wood from fully decomposing. Over time, this creates a thick layer of acidic peat. Peat swamp forests are typically surrounded by lowland rain forests on better-drained soils, and by brackish or salt-water mangrove forests near the coast."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/2007-09-20-57-kalimantan-foresta.jpg/330px-2007-09-20-57-kalimantan-foresta.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peat_swamp_forest","wikidata":"Q2352401"},{"title":"Freshwater swamp forest","blocks":[{"text":"Freshwater swamp forests, or flooded forests, are forests which are inundated with freshwater, either permanently or seasonally. They normally occur along the lower reaches of rivers and around freshwater lakes. Freshwater swamp forests are found in a range of climate zones, from boreal through temperate and subtropical to tropical."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Morava%27s_flooded_forest_02.jpg/330px-Morava%27s_flooded_forest_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Freshwater_swamp_forest","wikidata":"Q1940784"},{"title":"Peat","blocks":[{"text":"Peat is an accumulation of partially decayed vegetation or organic matter. It is unique to natural areas called peatlands, bogs, mires, moors, or muskegs. Sphagnum moss, also called peat moss, is one of the most common components in peat, although many other plants can contribute. The biological features of sphagnum mosses act to create a habitat aiding peat formation, a phenomenon termed 'habitat manipulation'. Soils consisting primarily of peat are known as histosols. Peat forms in wetland conditions, where flooding or stagnant water obstructs the flow of oxygen from the atmosphere, slowing the rate of decomposition. Peat properties such as organic matter content and saturated hydraulic conductivity can exhibit high spatial heterogeneity."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Peat_%2849302157252%29.jpg/330px-Peat_%2849302157252%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peat","wikidata":"Q184624"},{"title":"Swamp","blocks":[{"text":"A swamp is a forested wetland. Swamps are considered to be transition zones because both land and water play a role in creating this environment. Swamps vary in size and are located all around the world. The water of a swamp may be fresh water, brackish water, or seawater. Freshwater swamps form along large rivers or lakes where they are critically dependent upon rainwater and seasonal flooding to maintain natural water level fluctuations. Saltwater swamps are found along tropical and subtropical coastlines. Some swamps have hammocks, or dry-land protrusions, covered by aquatic vegetation, or vegetation that tolerates periodic inundation or soil saturation. The two main types of swamp are \"true\" or swamp forests and \"transitional\" or shrub swamps. In the boreal regions of Canada, the word swamp is colloquially used for what is more formally termed a bog, fen, or muskeg. Some of the world's largest swamps are found along major rivers such as the Amazon, the Mississippi, and the Congo."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Florida_freshwater_swamp_usgov_image.jpg/330px-Florida_freshwater_swamp_usgov_image.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Swamp","wikidata":"Q166735"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/September_1%2C_2026_UTC%2C_Southeast_Asia_Haze_NOAA_Imagery.jpg/500px-September_1%2C_2026_UTC%2C_Southeast_Asia_Haze_NOAA_Imagery.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/September_1%2C_2026_UTC%2C_Southeast_Asia_Haze_NOAA_Imagery.jpg/1280px-September_1%2C_2026_UTC%2C_Southeast_Asia_Haze_NOAA_Imagery.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/September_1%2C_2026_UTC%2C_Southeast_Asia_Haze_NOAA_Imagery.jpg/500px-September_1%2C_2026_UTC%2C_Southeast_Asia_Haze_NOAA_Imagery.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASeptember_1%2C_2026_UTC%2C_Southeast_Asia_Haze_NOAA_Imagery.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/Borneo_fires_and_smoke%2C_2002.jpg/500px-Bo